== 3. mtf\_cam (pyflate)


=== 3.1 Hardware description

Move-to-front + RUNA/RUNB run-expansion engine. SystemVerilog: #raw("rtl/mtf_cam.sv") (top) plus, in the same #raw("rtl/") folder, #raw("mtf_list") (256-entry move-to-front list, a parallel shift register read by rank), #raw("mtf_ctrl") (invocation/init-fill FSM), #raw("mtf_run") (RLE counter), #raw("mtf_expand") (run→byte), #raw("mtf_pack") (W-lane packer), #raw("item_fifo"), #raw("mtf_regs"). Single clock, #raw("rst_n").


=== 3.2 Inputs / outputs, widths, frequency

- #strong[I/O:] input is a #emph[rank]; the decoder indexes the alphabet, shifts preceding entries, and expands RUNA/RUNB groups through a buffered output packer #strong[8 bytes wide]. Interfaces (#raw("docs/mas.md §2")): 32-bit AXI4-Lite control/status window; 32-bit AXI4-Stream symbol beats in (#raw("s_axis_sym"), TLAST on the end-of-block beat); 64-bit (8·W, W = 8) AXI4-Stream out (#raw("m_axis_l")) with 8-bit TKEEP and TLAST; 1-bit interrupt.
- #strong[Operating frequency:] target #strong[50 MHz] (uArch §6). Achievable #strong[≈ 37.5 MHz] — #emph[post-CTS STA] at a 27 ns constraint that the design #strong[meets] (tt, evidence #raw("synth/evidence/tight27_ws.max.rpt"): +0.3066 ns worst setup slack, +0.195 ns hold → 26.69 ns). The 20 ns (50 MHz) run #strong[failed] by 6.5964 ns (#raw("synth/evidence/ws.max.rpt")); the 37.6 MHz that run back-computes agrees with the met run within 0.4 % and is quoted only as a cross-check. Missed 50 MHz by \~1.33×.

=== 3.3 Architecture

#raw("docs/uarch.md"): a 256×8 shift-register CAM with a 256:1 rank read-mux and a parallel registered move-to-front shift (every entry writable each cycle, so no RAM). Run expansion feeds a W=8-lane packer. K3 = #strong[1.063] cyc/sym (model) / #strong[1.0686] measured on the DUT.


=== 3.4 HW/SW interface

- Ranks in / L-vector bytes out; output DMA drains #strong[336,184] L-vector bytes (#raw("docs/integration.md")). Driver #raw("driver/mtf_cam_driver.py"), register-map verified (0 diffs), RTL-cosim 16/16 pass.

=== 3.5 Acceleration justification + estimate

- #strong[Baseline] #raw("T") = #strong[1,123.49 ms] (mean ≈ 1.12 s), #raw("results/timing_distributions.txt:6").
- #strong[Fraction] #raw("f") = #strong[0.1344] (#raw("move_to_front") self-time share, #raw("results/profile_functions.txt:60"), #raw("report_pyflate") §2).
- #strong[HW cost:] DUT-measured #strong[158,441 cycles] (K3 = 1.0686) → #strong[≈ 4.23 ms] \@ 37.5 MHz; model 157,560 cycles (K3 = 1.063) at W=8 (#raw("docs/ppa.md §3.1"), #raw("docs/integration.md")). Both cycle figures are disclosed; the DUT number carries implementation overhead over the model.
- Standalone Amdahl ceiling at f = 0.1344: 1.16× — the stage share is small, which is the argument for chaining it on chip rather than for a separate accelerator. \*\*Superseded by §3.8:\*\* measured as a chain at the Rust boundary, the hardware replaces the optimized Python symbol loop ≈ 28× faster and runs ≈ 1.3× slower than the Rust kernel at the achievable clock; end to end ≈ 6.6× vs the original (a tie with Python + Rust). The isolated-stage ratio (80.4 ms original MTF microbench → 19.0× \@ 37.5 MHz / 25.4× \@ 50 MHz, PRD K5) is a \*\*different experiment\*\* from the whole-decoder profile and must not be substituted for it.

